WEBVTT

00:00:01.020 --> 00:00:02.690
Won’t you win?

00:00:03.860 --> 00:00:04.730
Kawachi...

00:00:05.070 --> 00:00:08.730
For now, all you have to do is make delicious bread.

00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:11.200
The best <i>Japan</i> ever.

00:00:17.700 --> 00:00:18.460
Okay.

00:00:19.240 --> 00:00:22.370
We’ll now begin the semifinals for the

00:00:22.370 --> 00:00:24.710
newcomers’ battle, A group.

00:00:29.250 --> 00:00:32.260
From the Southern Tokyo Branch:
Azuma Kazuma.

00:00:32.260 --> 00:00:35.050
From the Pantasia Main Store:
Suwabara Kai.

00:00:35.050 --> 00:00:36.090
Step forward.

00:00:41.140 --> 00:00:43.270
Come on, Azuma, move it.

00:00:45.060 --> 00:00:46.230
I’ll do it...

00:00:47.360 --> 00:00:48.270
Did you say something?

00:00:49.480 --> 00:00:50.980
I’ll make it.

00:00:51.610 --> 00:00:52.990
For Tsukino’s sake...

00:00:53.660 --> 00:00:54.990
for Kawachi’s sake...

00:00:55.530 --> 00:00:57.990
and for the sake of Southern Tokyo Branch,

00:00:58.700 --> 00:01:01.750
the experimental, historical,
supreme <i>Japan</i>.

00:01:03.420 --> 00:01:06.000
<i>Japan</i> #44.

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:10.340
There’s English bread, German bread, and French bread,

00:01:10.340 --> 00:01:12.220
but Japan’s bread, <i>Japan</i>, does not exist.

00:01:12.220 --> 00:01:14.510
In that case, there’s no choice but to create it.

00:01:14.510 --> 00:01:18.020
This story is a serious, biographical ballad of a boy who possesses Solar Hands,

00:01:18.020 --> 00:01:23.140
Azuma Kazuma, who will create a Japanese bread made by and for the Japanese people,

00:01:23.140 --> 00:01:26.820
which can be presented to the world proudly.

00:01:37.450 --> 00:01:44.090
Somewhere far away, there are people listening carefully.

00:01:45.420 --> 00:01:52.060
In every place, there are people looking up at the sky.

00:01:53.180 --> 00:01:59.930
Under the night sky, we, who are whistling...

00:02:00.980 --> 00:02:07.650
without words, are just tracing constellations with our fingers.

00:02:07.900 --> 00:02:15.120
The dreams of the cold-sensitive... Your cold hands...

00:02:16.160 --> 00:02:24.500
The warming magic is to believe in one path.

00:02:24.960 --> 00:02:33.260
The single star found on the other side of the comet cloud...

00:02:33.510 --> 00:02:37.520
whether it be a shining or a faint star...

00:02:37.730 --> 00:02:40.510
is the light of only you.

00:02:40.810 --> 00:02:44.260
On the other side of the cloud in your heart,

00:02:44.260 --> 00:02:49.070
is a sign post that remains unseen.

00:02:49.530 --> 00:02:56.790
Now, opening these hands, what will you believe in today?

00:02:58.950 --> 00:03:01.160
The experimental, historical, supreme bread!

00:03:01.160 --> 00:03:03.380
It’s <i>Japan</i> #44!

00:03:05.990 --> 00:03:07.240
Azuma...

00:03:07.670 --> 00:03:09.000
Azuma-san.

00:03:09.800 --> 00:03:12.010
Tsukino, hand over the plank on your back.

00:03:12.010 --> 00:03:13.000
Okay!

00:03:17.560 --> 00:03:18.590
I’m off.

00:03:20.310 --> 00:03:20.800
Okay.

00:03:30.900 --> 00:03:32.520
Looks like you’re finally ready.

00:03:33.530 --> 00:03:34.570
That’s a pretty good expression, you...

00:03:34.570 --> 00:03:35.540
I’m sorry, Suwabara.
That’s a pretty good expression, you...

00:03:35.540 --> 00:03:36.520
I’m sorry, Suwabara.

00:03:37.080 --> 00:03:39.780
I’m winning this match.

00:03:41.910 --> 00:03:43.290
What was that?

00:03:43.290 --> 00:03:46.080
I’m right in front of him, and...

00:03:46.080 --> 00:03:48.040
Where’s that confidence coming from?

00:03:48.040 --> 00:03:50.870
Or is he challenging me in search of a weakness, and...

00:04:02.270 --> 00:04:04.560
Be strong, Suwabara Kai.

00:04:04.560 --> 00:04:06.520
You’re supposed to be the strongest newcomer.

00:04:06.520 --> 00:04:09.410
You can’t possibly lose in fighting spirit.

00:04:17.570 --> 00:04:19.280
S-Steam is rising from his hands!

00:04:19.870 --> 00:04:22.410
Smoke that’s falling to the ground...

00:04:22.410 --> 00:04:24.160
That’s dry ice.

00:04:24.160 --> 00:04:25.280
Dry ice, you say?

00:04:26.670 --> 00:04:30.460
Azuma, this is one of the
results of my waterfall training.

00:04:30.460 --> 00:04:33.620
Solar Gauntlet Overcoat!

00:04:33.620 --> 00:04:36.540
This is dangerous so under no circumstances should you imitate him!

00:04:36.540 --> 00:04:36.550
Overcoat?
This is dangerous so under no circumstances should you imitate him!

00:04:36.550 --> 00:04:37.920
Overcoat?

00:04:38.680 --> 00:04:40.510
I wonder if it means to put a Solar Gauntlet

00:04:40.510 --> 00:04:44.230
on top of the original Solar Gauntlet...

00:04:44.230 --> 00:04:45.440
Don’t be stupid.

00:04:45.440 --> 00:04:47.440
What kind of an overcoat is it
when you cool down your hands...?

00:04:47.440 --> 00:04:49.140
Think about it a little more carefully.

00:04:50.570 --> 00:04:52.400
What happens when you cool down your hands?

00:04:52.400 --> 00:04:53.390
What?

00:04:53.900 --> 00:04:56.100
Well, don’t they get... cold?

00:04:56.610 --> 00:04:57.940
Temporarily, yes.

00:04:58.490 --> 00:05:01.450
However, human beings have an
instinctive self-defense mechanism.

00:05:01.450 --> 00:05:03.200
If the extremities of your hands go cold,

00:05:03.200 --> 00:05:05.740
a large quantity of blood begins to
flow there in order to warm them.

00:05:05.740 --> 00:05:09.210
Moreover, what he’s holding there is dry ice!

00:05:09.210 --> 00:05:11.380
He probably has frostbite on his hands.

00:05:11.380 --> 00:05:12.870
They’re emitting smoke!

00:05:14.460 --> 00:05:17.110
What a scary man Suwabara is...

00:05:17.110 --> 00:05:20.200
to go so far as to burn himself to win...

00:05:20.200 --> 00:05:21.840
That’s some ferocious tenacity.

00:05:23.010 --> 00:05:24.970
While I was being pounded by the waterfall,

00:05:25.520 --> 00:05:28.230
I realized that in order to attain the true shine,

00:05:28.230 --> 00:05:31.810
heating alone is insufficient; you also need to cool it.

00:05:33.690 --> 00:05:35.180
What do you think now, Azuma?

00:05:35.180 --> 00:05:38.570
With this, my hands will surpass your Solar Hands.

00:05:38.570 --> 00:05:40.950
You can’t take it easy anymore.

00:05:40.950 --> 00:05:41.710
Suwabara...
You can’t take it easy anymore.

00:05:41.710 --> 00:05:42.270
Suwabara...

00:05:42.950 --> 00:05:44.740
I’m really sorry.

00:05:46.410 --> 00:05:49.970
I realized it when Kawachi lost.

00:05:51.130 --> 00:05:55.790
Unlike me, everyone really put
all they had into this competition.

00:05:55.790 --> 00:05:57.750
They were all thinking that they didn’t want to lose.

00:06:03.390 --> 00:06:04.430
But...

00:06:04.430 --> 00:06:06.730
even I can’t afford to lose.

00:06:06.730 --> 00:06:08.010
So, I’m sorry.

00:06:10.190 --> 00:06:13.690
I, Suwabara Kai, have aspired to
be a bread artisan since childhood.

00:06:13.690 --> 00:06:16.190
I’ve won countless contests...

00:06:16.190 --> 00:06:19.030
To think that you would insult me so much...

00:06:19.030 --> 00:06:21.480
I’m not going to let you leave here alive.

00:06:22.120 --> 00:06:23.440
Look!

00:06:23.990 --> 00:06:26.040
This is only 0.1mm thick.

00:06:26.040 --> 00:06:28.200
The Ultimate Solar Dough.

00:06:28.750 --> 00:06:30.420
What kind of thinness is that?

00:06:30.420 --> 00:06:31.670
It’s even thinner than

00:06:31.670 --> 00:06:34.750
the 324-layer croissant Solar Dough

00:06:34.750 --> 00:06:36.640
that Azuma made.

00:06:37.840 --> 00:06:40.940
I believe you were at 324 layers, right?

00:06:41.430 --> 00:06:45.220
But first, I fold into two, then into
three, and then into three twice more...

00:06:45.220 --> 00:06:46.470
54 layers.

00:06:46.470 --> 00:06:49.650
With this, I get the 54 layers of a regular croissant.

00:06:50.310 --> 00:06:52.680
From here, I further...

00:06:52.680 --> 00:06:56.690
fold it once more into three, and
then into two for 324 layers!

00:06:56.690 --> 00:06:59.430
He’s at 324 layers, just like Azuma!

00:06:59.430 --> 00:07:01.190
From there, I further...

00:07:01.660 --> 00:07:05.860
double it, to attain 648 layers!

00:07:09.200 --> 00:07:11.110
However, that’s not the end of it.

00:07:13.330 --> 00:07:18.830
This dough is then kept at -20°C, a temperature at which even a banana would freeze.

00:07:19.130 --> 00:07:20.830
Then, it’s baked at 400°C,

00:07:21.830 --> 00:07:23.970
twice the regular temperature,

00:07:23.970 --> 00:07:25.840
to cause vapor action.

00:07:26.390 --> 00:07:28.390
Vapor action, in the first place,

00:07:28.390 --> 00:07:31.850
is like an explosion caused by the difference in
temperatures between the dough and the oven.

00:07:31.850 --> 00:07:34.270
You used this at the preliminaries, too.

00:07:34.270 --> 00:07:36.560
However, you never thought to increase

00:07:36.560 --> 00:07:39.400
the temperature from the
extremities of -20°C to 400°C...

00:07:39.400 --> 00:07:41.600
You probably just don’t have enough skill.

00:07:54.920 --> 00:07:57.210
You see this end product?

00:07:57.210 --> 00:07:59.580
By cooling it to -20°C,

00:07:59.580 --> 00:08:03.430
it doesn’t even turn into an
atrocious charred croissant like yours.

00:08:03.430 --> 00:08:05.290
This wonderful luster...

00:08:06.010 --> 00:08:09.220
This is, without a doubt, the Earth’s best croissant,

00:08:09.220 --> 00:08:12.300
Super Vapor-Action Croissant,

00:08:12.300 --> 00:08:14.340
Six Hundred Forty-Eight!

00:08:14.340 --> 00:08:15.530
Croissant
Six Hundred Forty-Eight!

00:08:15.530 --> 00:08:16.560
Croissant

00:08:17.610 --> 00:08:19.060
Hey...

00:08:19.730 --> 00:08:21.070
Examiner Kuroyanagi.

00:08:21.650 --> 00:08:23.270
Would you mind sampling this first?

00:08:23.740 --> 00:08:26.270
Oh, you’re already done?

00:08:27.240 --> 00:08:28.750
They’ll get cold.

00:08:30.370 --> 00:08:31.530
Very well.

00:08:35.330 --> 00:08:36.800
H-He’s not listening.

00:08:38.710 --> 00:08:39.990
What’s happening?

00:08:40.840 --> 00:08:42.510
That filthy cockroach.

00:08:43.210 --> 00:08:45.340
I thought that he was going to self-destruct,

00:08:45.340 --> 00:08:48.750
but he suddenly got back onto
his feet and... he’s pretty calm.

00:08:49.600 --> 00:08:50.720
Who knows...

00:08:50.720 --> 00:08:53.890
Don’t “who knows” me.

00:08:53.890 --> 00:08:56.760
You’re smart, so explain it to me.

00:09:01.400 --> 00:09:03.150
But, it’s mysterious...

00:09:03.150 --> 00:09:06.480
Suwabara’s croissant is probably of quite a high level.

00:09:07.320 --> 00:09:11.730
Contrary to that, Azuma’s bread doesn’t
seem to have anything special about it.

00:09:12.830 --> 00:09:16.240
The only reason he could be so calm is...

00:09:18.380 --> 00:09:21.950
that plank he placed inside the oven.

00:09:23.960 --> 00:09:26.290
Dave has... Dave has...

00:09:27.130 --> 00:09:32.550
Dave has stood, and then died!

00:09:33.260 --> 00:09:34.770
K-Kuroyanagi-san!

00:09:35.310 --> 00:09:36.550
Kuroyanagi-san!

00:09:36.550 --> 00:09:39.550
It’s no use, Kuroyanagi-san’s the same.

00:09:40.150 --> 00:09:42.390
His breathing and pulse have stopped.

00:09:42.860 --> 00:09:44.140
What?!

00:09:45.900 --> 00:09:47.650
Call an ambulance, quickly!

00:09:50.120 --> 00:09:51.360
What is this?

00:09:52.080 --> 00:09:53.360
Azuma-kun...

00:09:54.990 --> 00:09:57.960
What in the world have you done with that bread,

00:09:59.120 --> 00:10:00.220
Azuma-kun...

00:10:10.720 --> 00:10:13.220
I’m Examiner Kuroyanagi Ryou.

00:10:13.840 --> 00:10:17.550
After sampling Azuma Kazuma’s bread,
because of it’s extreme deliciousness...

00:10:18.010 --> 00:10:19.520
I died.

00:10:26.690 --> 00:10:28.530
22 years...

00:10:28.530 --> 00:10:31.810
It was a short life, but I have no regrets.

00:10:32.860 --> 00:10:34.740
Because before I died,

00:10:34.740 --> 00:10:37.570
I was able to taste such a delicious bread at least once.

00:10:38.160 --> 00:10:41.030
Goodbye, and thank you...

00:10:41.660 --> 00:10:43.000
Azuma Kazuma.

00:10:50.630 --> 00:10:52.540
Th... This is...

00:10:53.470 --> 00:10:55.390
Could this be heaven?

00:10:55.390 --> 00:10:57.550
Heaven really does exist!

00:10:59.560 --> 00:11:01.550
Tiny birds are chirping.

00:11:01.980 --> 00:11:04.050
Flowers are blooming in profusion.

00:11:05.020 --> 00:11:07.060
The animals play out a love song.

00:11:11.610 --> 00:11:14.060
This really feels comfortable.

00:11:16.280 --> 00:11:21.070
However, what in the world is that
place with a suspicious feel to it?

00:11:21.070 --> 00:11:25.070
Heaven
Cabaret Club

00:11:27.500 --> 00:11:29.160
Hey there, Mister!

00:11:31.630 --> 00:11:33.380
Would you like to stop by first?

00:11:33.380 --> 00:11:36.180
It’s the stop-by heaven for those
who’ve been here for 15 minutes.

00:11:37.640 --> 00:11:40.880
No, such places aren’t really my...

00:11:40.880 --> 00:11:43.220
Don’t be a prude.

00:11:43.220 --> 00:11:45.010
You have nothing else to do, right?

00:11:45.010 --> 00:11:45.930
And...

00:11:45.930 --> 00:11:48.930
your friend seems to really want to come.

00:11:49.360 --> 00:11:51.440
Ah, seems like fun, seems like fun...

00:11:53.030 --> 00:11:56.700
For sure, it is not like I have any other place to go to...

00:11:56.700 --> 00:11:59.440
This is the first time that I’ve ever
been to heaven, after all...

00:11:59.780 --> 00:12:02.330
And this girl, Satsuki...

00:12:02.330 --> 00:12:05.030
resembles Cathy a little.

00:12:07.000 --> 00:12:08.080
All right!

00:12:08.080 --> 00:12:09.450
Everything is an experience!

00:12:10.790 --> 00:12:12.960
Two deceased, coming in!

00:12:22.220 --> 00:12:24.770
Is it okay if I lie on your tummy?

00:12:25.730 --> 00:12:27.650
Sure, sure.

00:12:29.400 --> 00:12:31.320
Sir, your name is...?

00:12:31.820 --> 00:12:32.940
Kuroyanagi Ryou.

00:12:32.940 --> 00:12:36.280
I see. Your name’s Kuroyanagi-san?

00:12:36.280 --> 00:12:38.400
Is it your first time in such a place?

00:12:38.400 --> 00:12:39.990
Well, yes...

00:12:39.990 --> 00:12:42.870
It’s the first time I ever went to heaven,

00:12:43.830 --> 00:12:45.450
Just relax.

00:12:47.370 --> 00:12:48.750
It’s okay.

00:12:48.750 --> 00:12:50.630
Relax, relax.

00:12:57.550 --> 00:12:58.800
Hey, hey...

00:12:58.800 --> 00:13:00.970
So, Kuroyanagi-san,
do you have a girlfriend?

00:13:05.140 --> 00:13:06.980
Three years ago,

00:13:06.980 --> 00:13:09.190
I had to return to Japan from America,

00:13:09.190 --> 00:13:10.740
so we had to separate.

00:13:11.060 --> 00:13:12.610
Not since then.

00:13:15.280 --> 00:13:17.160
She was a beautiful woman.

00:13:17.820 --> 00:13:19.370
She had blonde hair.

00:13:19.780 --> 00:13:23.360
She’d always gaze at me with clear eyes.

00:13:23.830 --> 00:13:24.820
That’s right.

00:13:25.410 --> 00:13:26.790
Satsuki!

00:13:26.790 --> 00:13:30.370
She’d gaze at me with a kind smile just like you.

00:13:30.960 --> 00:13:32.510
You look like her,

00:13:32.920 --> 00:13:33.830
like Cathy.

00:13:35.000 --> 00:13:36.080
So, you mean...?

00:13:37.960 --> 00:13:40.100
It means that you’re also beautiful.

00:13:42.090 --> 00:13:43.770
Kuroyanagi-san...

00:13:45.970 --> 00:13:48.060
I understand, though... just that,

00:13:48.060 --> 00:13:51.770
it’s an annoyance for you to be loved by a man who

00:13:51.770 --> 00:13:53.730
died from eating bread, but...

00:13:53.730 --> 00:13:55.480
That’s not true.

00:13:55.820 --> 00:13:58.200
I like you, too, Kuroyanagi-san...

00:13:59.030 --> 00:13:59.980
Satsuki...

00:14:05.660 --> 00:14:06.490
But...

00:14:06.870 --> 00:14:08.990
“But”? What is it?

00:14:15.380 --> 00:14:17.050
He probably can’t be saved.

00:14:17.050 --> 00:14:18.710
You might want to contact his relatives...

00:14:20.670 --> 00:14:23.170
No! Dave!

00:14:23.890 --> 00:14:26.180
Why has it turned out like this...?

00:14:26.180 --> 00:14:27.010
I don’t know.

00:14:27.010 --> 00:14:27.880
However...

00:14:28.520 --> 00:14:32.430
There’s no mistaking that two
people have died from Azuma’s bread.

00:14:34.900 --> 00:14:35.980
Azuma,

00:14:35.980 --> 00:14:38.640
what have you done?

00:14:40.280 --> 00:14:41.950
Azuma, you bastard!

00:14:41.950 --> 00:14:45.190
Did you add poison to the bread when you
thought that you couldn’t win the match?

00:14:46.910 --> 00:14:49.240
You dirty bastard.

00:14:49.240 --> 00:14:52.210
You didn’t want to lose to me so much that
you had to resort to something like this?

00:14:52.210 --> 00:14:52.910
Please stop this.

00:14:53.750 --> 00:14:55.470
General Manager...

00:14:56.580 --> 00:14:59.920
I hope we can get an explanation as to what this is.

00:14:59.920 --> 00:15:02.130
If not, even we will have to assume

00:15:02.130 --> 00:15:04.220
that this is a murder, and call the poli...

00:15:04.220 --> 00:15:04.810
They’re not dead.
that this is a murder, and call the poli...

00:15:04.810 --> 00:15:05.670
They’re not dead.

00:15:07.930 --> 00:15:10.470
You can’t die from bread, can you?

00:15:10.470 --> 00:15:12.680
And of course, I haven’t put any poison in.

00:15:14.020 --> 00:15:15.940
However, they’ve gone to heaven,

00:15:15.940 --> 00:15:16.680
that’s all.

00:15:18.480 --> 00:15:20.440
What does that mean...?

00:15:20.860 --> 00:15:22.150
No, it’s just that...

00:15:22.150 --> 00:15:24.280
<i>Japan</i> #44 is...

00:15:24.280 --> 00:15:27.900
really good, so occasionally
people who eat it go to heaven.

00:15:28.580 --> 00:15:30.240
They’ll come back soon enough,

00:15:30.240 --> 00:15:31.410
so don’t worry.

00:15:31.410 --> 00:15:34.160
He says, “So don’t worry”...

00:15:40.300 --> 00:15:42.420
Why, Satsuki?!

00:15:42.420 --> 00:15:45.880
If we both like each other,
shouldn’t we just stay together naturally?

00:15:48.050 --> 00:15:49.890
I’m now a dead man.

00:15:49.890 --> 00:15:52.520
I won’t put you through the same pain as Cathy.

00:15:52.850 --> 00:15:55.890
I will love only you, and live here forever.

00:15:56.190 --> 00:15:59.610
I’m so happy that you’d even say
such a thing that I could die...

00:15:59.610 --> 00:16:01.110
If I wasn’t already dead...

00:16:01.110 --> 00:16:03.580
But... it’s impossible.

00:16:04.400 --> 00:16:07.910
Because, you’re not dead yet.

00:16:08.910 --> 00:16:10.650
What?!

00:16:11.120 --> 00:16:11.790
See that?

00:16:11.790 --> 00:16:14.870
Your body’s slowly beginning to disappear.

00:16:18.670 --> 00:16:22.120
Recently, an old man named Azuma Umasaburou

00:16:22.120 --> 00:16:27.130
came here after eating some #44 bread.

00:16:28.090 --> 00:16:29.760
He was a little perverted,

00:16:29.760 --> 00:16:32.390
but he was a really kind old man.

00:16:32.390 --> 00:16:35.100
I never had a grandfather,

00:16:35.100 --> 00:16:38.350
so it was like I had a real grandfather, and I was happy.

00:16:38.350 --> 00:16:39.360
But...

00:16:40.610 --> 00:16:45.570
People who haven’t lived
out their lives go back to Earth.

00:16:45.570 --> 00:16:47.900
Of course, the same goes for you...

00:16:48.780 --> 00:16:49.910
Satsuki...

00:16:49.910 --> 00:16:51.660
I know...

00:16:51.660 --> 00:16:54.620
If you get close to someone
who’s not yet lived out their life,

00:16:54.620 --> 00:16:57.120
then you must part... It’s painful.

00:16:58.040 --> 00:17:00.380
I just hadn’t noticed.

00:17:00.380 --> 00:17:02.370
I really thought I was dead...

00:17:06.670 --> 00:17:09.840
Then, at least for as long as this body remains,

00:17:09.840 --> 00:17:11.130
I want to hold you.

00:17:29.610 --> 00:17:31.280
Kuroyanagi-san,

00:17:31.280 --> 00:17:34.110
please live well.

00:17:41.210 --> 00:17:42.830
They didn’t pay.

00:17:45.170 --> 00:17:48.050
It does not look like they will come back to life.

00:17:49.470 --> 00:17:52.760
I do not think that this boy would murder someone,

00:17:52.760 --> 00:17:54.550
but calling the police is probably...

00:18:08.650 --> 00:18:10.530
In case of such a situation,

00:18:10.530 --> 00:18:14.190
I had my mask set to cover my entire face.

00:18:15.370 --> 00:18:17.450
M-M-M-M... Mei-Mei-Mei-Mei-Mei...

00:18:17.950 --> 00:18:19.910
He really came back to life...

00:18:19.910 --> 00:18:21.050
Mei-Mei-Mei...

00:18:23.120 --> 00:18:23.950
Yo.

00:18:24.460 --> 00:18:26.000
Azuma!

00:18:26.380 --> 00:18:27.590
You’re the victor!

00:18:27.590 --> 00:18:30.000
You’ve really made a bread delicious enough to die for!

00:18:31.460 --> 00:18:32.710
What?!

00:18:33.470 --> 00:18:35.350
Wait, Kuroyanagi!

00:18:35.350 --> 00:18:38.680
To suddenly come back to life, and to
suddenly decide the results of the match...

00:18:38.680 --> 00:18:40.140
What do you mean by this?

00:18:40.140 --> 00:18:42.690
You haven’t sampled my bread yet,

00:18:42.690 --> 00:18:44.930
and Dave’s phonetic points aren’t here yet!

00:18:46.110 --> 00:18:49.190
I believe that Dave-sensei already shares my feelings.

00:18:49.190 --> 00:18:50.110
What?!

00:18:51.740 --> 00:18:56.110
“The girl with Kuroyanagi was my type as well”?

00:18:57.530 --> 00:18:59.860
I don’t... understand...

00:19:02.120 --> 00:19:03.540
Shut up, shut up.

00:19:03.540 --> 00:19:06.290
Just eat my croissant without saying anything.

00:19:06.290 --> 00:19:07.370
If you do so...

00:19:07.920 --> 00:19:09.460
Will I be able to go to heaven?

00:19:10.300 --> 00:19:11.350
What?!

00:19:12.510 --> 00:19:16.460
Dave-sensei and I went to
heaven because of Azuma’s bread.

00:19:17.260 --> 00:19:19.720
As long as I can’t go to heaven with your bread...

00:19:19.720 --> 00:19:20.970
it’s your loss.

00:19:25.520 --> 00:19:26.940
Don’t be depressed.

00:19:26.940 --> 00:19:29.100
It’s not like you’re weak...

00:19:29.100 --> 00:19:30.690
It’s just that Azuma is really strong.

00:19:31.690 --> 00:19:34.410
But, I really can’t be satisfied with this...

00:19:34.990 --> 00:19:37.650
At least let me have a bite of Azuma’s bread...

00:19:37.650 --> 00:19:38.900
Not possible!

00:19:39.530 --> 00:19:44.410
I’ve already decided that I’m going
to take the rest for further research.

00:19:44.410 --> 00:19:46.910
No matter what anyone says,
I won’t hand it over to anyone!

00:19:47.420 --> 00:19:48.840
Kuroyanagi-san!

00:19:48.840 --> 00:19:51.750
Dave-sensei and Azuma
Kazuma’s bread have disappeared.

00:19:51.750 --> 00:19:52.540
What?!

00:19:58.930 --> 00:19:59.720
After him!

00:19:59.720 --> 00:20:02.220
Retrieve <i>Japan</i> #44 at all costs!

00:20:02.220 --> 00:20:03.510
Yes, sir!

00:20:03.850 --> 00:20:05.600
You...

00:20:05.600 --> 00:20:08.010
You fat, greedy pig of an author.

00:20:08.310 --> 00:20:10.570
I can just make another of those.

00:20:10.570 --> 00:20:12.840
I can’t promise that you’ll go to heaven again, though.

00:20:12.840 --> 00:20:13.520
Really?

00:20:14.690 --> 00:20:15.740
No...

00:20:16.650 --> 00:20:17.520
Anyway...

00:20:17.910 --> 00:20:20.830
It was amazing, Azuma Kazuma.

00:20:20.830 --> 00:20:23.030
But, what’s the secret behind it?

00:20:23.030 --> 00:20:26.580
I had my grandpa explain something to me,

00:20:26.580 --> 00:20:28.540
but truthfully, even I don’t quite understand.

00:20:29.290 --> 00:20:33.210
Either way, I put that plank in the oven before baking...

00:20:33.210 --> 00:20:35.540
Apparently, it’s called Petalite.

00:20:36.010 --> 00:20:37.580
Petalite?

00:20:37.580 --> 00:20:38.800
Youchouseki?

00:20:38.800 --> 00:20:40.260
The asashouryuzeki?

00:20:40.850 --> 00:20:42.600
No, youchouseki.

00:20:43.060 --> 00:20:46.270
It’s even called the “Magical Stone.”
Its English name is Petalite.

00:20:46.730 --> 00:20:50.390
Its characteristic is that it can reflect infrared
radiation over ten times better than regular iron.

00:20:50.980 --> 00:20:52.610
If you bake bread in a stone oven,

00:20:52.610 --> 00:20:54.940
it concentrates infrared radiation to a high degree,

00:20:54.940 --> 00:20:57.450
and that alone gives rise to delicious bread.

00:20:57.450 --> 00:21:02.400
However, that plank probably
concentrates more radiation than stone.

00:21:02.780 --> 00:21:05.910
I don’t quite understand, but that’s probably it, right?

00:21:06.410 --> 00:21:09.210
Long ago, when I asked my
Grandpa Umasaburou from Gifu

00:21:09.210 --> 00:21:13.410
how I could bake bread as if it was in a stone oven...

00:21:13.410 --> 00:21:14.800
he made this for me.

00:21:18.550 --> 00:21:19.580
Umasaburou...?

00:21:19.580 --> 00:21:21.130
I’ve heard this name from somewhere...

00:21:21.970 --> 00:21:22.670
Azuma!

00:21:23.430 --> 00:21:24.560
You did it!

00:21:24.560 --> 00:21:25.970
Amazing!

00:21:25.970 --> 00:21:27.850
You’re really a genius.

00:21:27.850 --> 00:21:29.940
That has nothing to do with it.

00:21:29.940 --> 00:21:32.680
“I’ll win.”

00:21:32.680 --> 00:21:34.320
I promised you that.

00:21:34.320 --> 00:21:35.600
So, I simply just didn’t want to lose.

00:21:36.480 --> 00:21:37.370
Azuma...

00:21:40.990 --> 00:21:42.490
It’s beautiful,

00:21:42.490 --> 00:21:43.830
love between friends.

00:21:43.830 --> 00:21:45.320
No matter how many times you see it, it’s refreshing.

00:21:46.240 --> 00:21:47.070
Yukino.

00:21:47.070 --> 00:21:49.710
I don’t know if we can win,

00:21:50.540 --> 00:21:52.580
but I’m really looking forward to the finals.

00:21:53.080 --> 00:21:55.330
You’re really looking forward to it?

00:21:56.170 --> 00:21:58.630
Aren’t you actually really scared?

00:21:58.630 --> 00:22:00.790
After seeing Azuma’s strength.

00:22:01.840 --> 00:22:02.840
You cockroach.

00:22:03.640 --> 00:22:04.550
Prepare yourself.

00:22:04.550 --> 00:22:06.220
Prepare...

00:22:06.220 --> 00:22:07.100
Okay.

00:22:07.100 --> 00:22:08.550
I’ll remember that.

00:22:08.550 --> 00:22:10.800
Prepare myself...?
Damn cockroach.

00:22:15.650 --> 00:22:18.990
It’s they who should be getting prepared.

00:22:18.990 --> 00:22:21.570
Right, boy?

00:22:21.570 --> 00:22:22.570
Yes, yes.

00:22:54.480 --> 00:22:56.240
On this chest, big and strong

00:22:56.240 --> 00:22:58.360
A look that glitters and doesn't lose.

00:22:58.360 --> 00:23:00.360
That's what I searched for, fumbling in the wind.

00:23:00.360 --> 00:23:01.660
The answer for now is...

00:23:01.660 --> 00:23:04.580
For now, I'll watch the situation and wait for a chance.
I got the patience to wait at a distance.

00:23:04.580 --> 00:23:06.370
A prisoner who just screams is no good.

00:23:06.370 --> 00:23:08.160
Just Follow Me! I'll lend you my shoulder occasionally.

00:23:17.010 --> 00:23:18.260
It's by no means a fleeting dream.

00:23:18.260 --> 00:23:21.140
Let this sentiment reach you. Heart to Heart, Soul to Soul.

00:23:21.140 --> 00:23:23.180
The seasons turn. Splendid as a spring storm.

00:23:23.180 --> 00:23:24.590
Win Big is the motto.

00:23:26.270 --> 00:23:29.390
Does a thing like eternity really exist?

00:23:29.390 --> 00:23:31.230
And so we... C'mon.

00:23:32.610 --> 00:23:36.780
Yeah, yeah, we live to touch the one shining moment.

00:23:53.710 --> 00:23:57.590
To all the soldiers fighting today using the tail wind...

00:24:05.510 --> 00:24:07.180
Yukino, prepare yourself.

00:24:07.180 --> 00:24:09.470
With Azuma’s <i>Japan</i> #44, you’re going to heaven...

00:24:09.470 --> 00:24:11.680
no, I mean hell!

00:24:11.680 --> 00:24:13.310
Oh, I’m so scared.

00:24:13.310 --> 00:24:14.560
What should I do?

00:24:14.560 --> 00:24:15.940
Next time, on Yakitate Japan!,

00:24:15.940 --> 00:24:17.310
Just before the finals!!

00:24:17.310 --> 00:24:18.810
The black shadow that approaches Kazuma!

00:24:18.810 --> 00:24:19.970
Be sure to watch.

00:24:20.480 --> 00:24:22.730
Yakitate!! Seed of knowledge.

00:24:22.730 --> 00:24:24.900
Azuma’s secret weapon, Petalite.

00:24:24.900 --> 00:24:26.860
It originates from the Greek
words for “leaf” and “stone.”

00:24:26.860 --> 00:24:29.120
If can stand high temperatures,
but it’s surprisingly fragile,

00:24:29.120 --> 00:24:31.740
and broken fragments of it resemble leaves.

00:24:32.080 --> 00:24:33.790
Really?
